---
import LabsLayout from "../../layouts/labs.astro";
---

<LabsLayout title="Scenario D — Single-root fan-out — Querial Labs" active="d">
    <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-querial-indigo-on-dark">Scenario D</p>
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mt-1">Single-root fan-out</h1>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-3">
                Teaching topology and failure policy. One extract is the only structural
                root. Both destination loads hang off it. SQL Server uses
                <code class="text-foreground">sql_command</code> with step
                <code class="text-foreground">failure_policy: continue</code>; PostgreSQL
                uses staged SQL from the same Parquet file.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <a href="/labs/adventureworks/downloads/scenario-d-fanout.zip" download
               class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg bg-querial-indigo px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-white hover:opacity-90">
                Download scenario-d-fanout.zip
            </a>
            <a href="/labs/run-through" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg border border-border/60 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-muted/50">
                Load and test
            </a>
            <a href="/docs/developer-pipelines" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg border border-border/60 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-muted/50">
                Failure policy
            </a>
        </div>

        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-6 [&>p]:text-muted-foreground [&>h2]:text-foreground">
            <h2>Package</h2>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
                <li>Package <code class="text-foreground">aw-scenario-d</code>, pipeline <code class="text-foreground">aw_scenario_d</code>.</li>
                <li>Same three stubs as C: source, sql-dest, pg-dest.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Topology</h2>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>extract_sales_order  (ROOT, parquet → aw-source)
  ├─(succeeded)──────────→ load_sales_order_sqlserver
  │                        sql_command, failure_policy continue, re-queries source
  └─(artifact_available)→ load_sales_order_postgres
                           staged-database-sql → aw-pg-dest</code></pre>
            <p>
                Unlike C, the SS load is <strong class="text-foreground">not</strong> a root.
                It waits for the extract to succeed even though it re-queries AdventureWorks
                instead of reading Parquet.
            </p>

            <h2>Migrations</h2>
            <p>Same dual chains as C (ss_001/ss_005 and pg_001/pg_005).</p>

            <h2>Failure policy</h2>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
                <li>SS load <code class="text-foreground">failure_policy: continue</code> — a MERGE failure does not latch run-wide fail-fast. Dependents that require success skip; the PG branch can still finish under run-level <code class="text-foreground">fail_fast</code>.</li>
                <li>Optionally set the deployment override to <code class="text-foreground">continue_independent</code> when experimenting with other <code class="text-foreground">fail_pipeline</code> steps.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                Experiment: point SS dest at a catalog without <code class="text-foreground">aw.sales_order</code>
                (or break the MERGE), keep PG healthy, trigger. Graph: extract Succeeded,
                SS Failed (continue), PG Succeeded. Run status may still be Failed because
                a step failed — read the inspector, not only the run badge.
            </p>

            <h2>Flags</h2>
            <p>PostgreSQL branch requires Artifacts + DuckDB.</p>

            <h2>Run Graph</h2>
            <p>
                Exactly one root badge. Fan-out visible as two edges from the extract.
                Click SS node: classification / failure policy continue. Click PG: artifact
                from the extract. Critical path is extract plus the slower sink.
            </p>

            <h2>Verify</h2>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>SELECT COUNT(*) FROM aw.sales_order;  -- on each destination</code></pre>
        </div>
    </div>
</LabsLayout>
